"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HN026","id":101128679,"login":"HN026","node_id":"U_kgDOBgcZ5w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026","user_view_type":"public"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HN026/gatewise/releases/assets/726510144"}],"assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HN026/gatewise/releases/438812760/assets","author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101128679?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HN026","id":101128679,"login":"HN026","node_id":"U_kgDOBgcZ5w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HN026","user_view_type":"public"},"body":"Gatewise v1.0.0 establishes the supported API and deployment contract while retaining existing configuration defaults.\n\n- Fixed a queue priority inversion found by the native ARM64 matrix. Capacity release and queue selection now advance atomically; application logging remains outside the queue lock. The ordering check passed 1,000 local repetitions and is repeated in CI.\n- Froze the exported API across eight public packages. Native Linux AMD64/ARM64 CI runs race tests, vet and builds with Go 1.22 and current stable Go; current-Go macOS ARM64 was checked locally.\n- Added native AMD64/ARM64 proxy image delivery with a pinned builder, non-root runtime, SBOM/provenance, runtime/overload/shutdown checks and vulnerability gates before the version tag is assembled.\n- Completed four three-minute PostgreSQL validation runs locally: 616,400 requests and 60 passing checks. The full protocol was also repeated on Linux CI. A separate two-second exploratory Linux smoke missed the 99% recovery target for background traffic (47/48 succeeded, one refused); its original report is retained. Results retain refusals, errors, latency misses, memory observations and recovery separately; they are not a production-capacity or long-term leak-free guarantee.\n- The exact downloadable demo passed 2,288 Postman assertions across 69 real-PostgreSQL profiles. Fresh module integration, practical rollout/rollback guidance and clearer design/benchmark/metrics documentation are included.\n\nNo configuration migration is required from v0.11.1. Immediate refusal and legacy adaptive feedback remain the defaults. Waiting and other policies remain opt-in. Use keyed Go configuration literals. Limits remain per engine/process; canceled proxy requests can finish before remote work stops.\n\nInstall: `go get github.com/HN026/gatewise@v1.0.0`\n\nImage: `ghcr.io/hn026/gatewise:v1.0.0` (Linux AMD64 and ARM64; publication follows the release workflow).\n\n[Installation](https://hn026.github.io/gatewise-site/#/installation) · [Compatibility contract](https://hn026.github.io/gatewise-site/#/reference/compatibility) · [Measured reliability](https://hn026.github.io/gatewise-site/#/benchmarks/reliability)\n","created_at":"2026-11-09T06:47:09Z","draft":false,"html_url":"https://github.com/HN026/gatewise/releases/tag/v1.0.0","id":438812760,"immutable":false,"name":"Gatewise v1.0.0"